I've been playing around with patching my copy of Nethack for
a few days now, and I have run into a question.

  I would like to modify the "flipcoin" patch so that while the
player is allowed to apply a coin to flip it, he won't see '$'
listed in the list of things he can by default (a)pply.
  Consider the behavior of (w)ield:

g - a blessed diamond.
What do you want to wield? [- abcd or ?*]
g - a blessed diamond (weapon in hand).

  I'd like the same behavior with coins and (a)pply as is
currently present with gems and (w)ield.  But I don't know
what I need to change to make this happen.  Could anyone
advise me?

  [Essentially, I'd like to make coin-flipping possible without
explicitly telling the player that he can do it.  It's one of
those actions that IMHO should be an "easter egg," and besides,
the $ clutters up the display in the majority of cases: when you
really want to (a)pply something useful.]

